  "family": "classical",
  "lineage": "Sinhala vannama Sri Lankan classical court dance-song tradition, comprising eighteen canonical pieces composed in the seventeenth-eighteenth centuries at the Kandyan royal court for performance at state ceremonies. Each of the eighteen vannamas evokes a specific subject (gaja-vannama elephant, ashva-vannama horse, mayura-vannama peacock, sinha-vannama lion, etc.) through characteristic melodic-and-rhythmic gesture and stylized choreographic movement. Performance combines solo male voice with geta-bera double-headed barrel drum and elaborate choreography. The Sri Lankan Cultural Department and Royal Asiatic Society preserve the canonical transmission.",
